# Flight modes for a THREE-position switch (FS-i6 SwC on channel 5).
#
# A 3-position switch does not reach six slots. At the usual 1000/1500/2000 us
# it lands in slots 1, 4 and 6 -- so those are the only three that matter, and
# the rest are filled with the same value as their neighbour so that PWM drift
# across a boundary changes nothing.
#
# CONFIRM with ./mode_monitor.py before trusting this. Endpoint and subtrim
# settings on the transmitter move the actual PWM, and if your switch lands in
# different slots this mapping is wrong for your radio.
#
#   slot 1  STABILIZE  manual, always available, what you learn on
#   slot 4  ALT_HOLD   holds height, still manual in the horizontal
#   slot 6  RTL        the recovery mode -- the reason a 3-position switch is
#                      worth having at all
#
# Once GPS is trusted and mounted on a mast, LOITER (5) is a reasonable swap
# for ALT_HOLD in the middle position.
FLTMODE1 0
FLTMODE2 0
FLTMODE3 2
FLTMODE4 2
FLTMODE5 6
FLTMODE6 6
